+```
+
+`BytecodeVm::pending_object` is one `Option`, and `DEF_OBJECT` overwrites it, so
+the inner declaration takes the outer's place; when the outer body then finishes,
+`finish_object` finds nothing left to assemble and the `expect` panics. The panic
+is pre-existing — the same `expect` is reached from `unwind_frame` on the tree's
+own path, and `git show HEAD:src/bytecode/vm.rs` panics on the same program — so
+nothing in this phase caused it.
+
+Fixing it means holding the declarations being assembled in a stack rather than in
+one slot, and threading the innermost through `has`/`to can` and `finish_object`,
+which is a change to the bytecode VM's object model and not a fix to this phase's
+defect. Round 2 added nothing here: `unwind_frames_above` registers the type of an
+`object` body it has to abandon, which is the same `finish_object` an ordinary
+exit uses and the same invariant — one pending declaration per body frame — the
+`expect` above already assumes.

